.4, "adr20" : 5.6, "dollar_volume" : 12469686, "sector" : "Technology", "themes" : []}]}}, "definitions" : {"session" : "A trading session is a date on which at least 3,000 common stocks or ADRs have a daily bar. Dates come from the data, never the clock.", "universe" : "Common stocks and ADRs that closed at 1.00 dollar or more on the newest session, with a 20-session median dollar volume of at least 5 million dollars (on at least 15 of the 20 sessions).", "return" : "Percent change of the close from 5, 21, 63 or 126 sessions before the newest session (1 week, 1 month, 3 months, 6 months) to the newest close. A stock without a bar on the base session is not ranked for that period.", "pct_from_high" : "The newest close against the highest daily high of the last 252 sessions, in percent (0 = at the high, negative = below it).", "adr20" : "Average daily range: the mean of high divided by low over the last 20 sessions, as a percent above 1.", "dollar_volume" : "Median of close times volume over the last 20 sessions.", "deal_pinned" : "Left out: a stock held at a buyout price. Each of the last 4 sessions traded inside 2 percent of the close, and within 180 days one day rose 15 percent or more on at least 10 times its 21-day average volume.", "sector" : "The nightly RS run's sector when the stock is in it, else the cached sector; empty when neither has one.", "themes" : "The active themes that hold the stock today (newest row per theme in the last 7 days, not Retired).", "not_claimed" : "Display only. Nothing here feeds a trade, a grade, an alert or any sizing."}}
